<PLAYER_SETUP>
  random_placement

<LAND_GENERATION>
  base_terrain GRASS

  create_player_lands
  {
    terrain_type GRASS
    land_percent 10
  }

<TERRAIN_GENERATION>

/* HOUSE create_terrain SNOW { base_terrain GRASS land_percent 100 } */

<OBJECTS_GENERATION>


/*
================================================================================
RMSTEST_82a - does a word whose engine number is 70 end a comment?
Feeds: docs/token-alias-design.md Sec.3.1 and slice B (the comment close).

The header is at the bottom on purpose, below every section. A test about
words that end comments must not put such words in its own header, so this
header names no constant whose number is a comment marker or a control word.

THE CASE. The terrain section holds one comment. Its first word is the object
whose number is 70, the number the RMS Equivalencies sheet gives the comment
close marker. After it comes a whole create_terrain painting SNOW over all
GRASS, then the real comment close.

PREDICTIONS, written 2026-11-02 before the run.
  - The word ends the comment: the create_terrain runs, the map is SNOW
    everywhere a player land or the base is, and the trailing comment close
    is a stray token the engine ignores.
  - It does not: the comment covers the line, the map is GRASS.
Read: probe_scenario.py, terrain histogram. SNOW above 0 means it ends.

Controls: 82b (an object word with another number, should be GRASS) and 82c
(the literal number 70, should be GRASS, as the literal 69 did nothing in
RMSTEST_57).

Generate at: Tiny, 2 players, seed 1000, scenario editor.
================================================================================
*/
